          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans SemiDemi'>Analysis of</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#e15759' fontname='Bodoni MT'> 50,000</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans SemiDemi'> Uber trip records across six major metropolitan markets</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#e15759' fontname='Bodoni MT'> (Boston, Chicago, Los Angeles, New York, San Francisco, and Seattle)</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans SemiDemi'> reveals a highly resilient revenue baseline paired with strategic optimization opportunities in trip duration, hourly demand shifts, and distance monetization yields.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#f28e2b' fontname='Courier New' fontsize='10'>Total Revenue    Completed Trips     Avg Yield/KM      Cancellation Rate</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#f28e2b' fontname='Courier New' fontsize='10'>  $679,685          42,540             $2.28/km              10.0% </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
